<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.13.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01488</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.13.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>22e47e21-32bd-4191-9db3-6f288341b1c4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="041e7b7b-8fff-402e-a72e-003fbf4a9742" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2db26d10-04e4-4540-a272-30228d06b376" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>Here is a graph of \(p\), an insect population, \(w\) weeks after it was first measured. The population
          grows exponentially. 
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/be8f4718ec44f2071d0a890cab99468e1bc5a1c2"/></media></figure><para>
              What is the weekly factor of growth for the insect population? </para>
          </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e8f10c0a-032d-4ab5-8933-ce06c9f51e2d" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="300">
    <problem>
      <para>What was the population when it was first measured? </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1ce-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cbfdb135-dc79-4528-bb35-0db6647ca15f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(p=300 \cdot 3^w\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(p=300+3^w\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p=300 \\cdot 3^w\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p= \\frac{300}{3^w}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(p=-300 \\cdot 3^w\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write an equation relating \(p\) and \(w\).</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="81c70864-a6bf-4d9e-83de-c1d4540d165c" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{9}{10}\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;0&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{9}{10}\\)&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, &quot;1.3&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{18}{5}\\) &quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here is a graph of the function \(f\) defined by \(f(x)=a \cdot b^x\). <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8557128fefac88efa9d2e444483c4358ec43784e"/></media></figure><emphasis>
            Select three </emphasis> possible values of \(b\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="20429ef0-bf0e-4a6b-8570-8d3531211391" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Graph 1" data-solution-options="[&quot;Graph 1&quot;, &quot;Graph 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The function \(f\) is given by \(f(x)=50\cdot (\frac{1}{2})^x\), and the function \(g\) is given by
          \(g(x)=50 \cdot (\frac{1}{3})^x\).
          Here are graphs of \(f\) and \(g\).
          
          <figure><media alt="Graph of two decreasing exponential functions, xy-plane, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6414b8e8e85d787caa65ad053cd0afa0f6c657ac"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.3 – 5.13.4. Are you using it
        the right way?
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bd2f7076-6229-4987-ad09-6ec00a25b88d" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="greater than" data-solution-options="[&quot;greater than&quot;, &quot;less than&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The function \(f\) is defined by \(f(x)=50 \cdot 3^x\). The function \(g\) is defined by \(g(x)=a
          \cdot b^x\).
          Here are graphs of \(f\) and \(g\).
          
          <figure><media alt="Graph of two increasing exponential functions, labeled f and g, xy-plane, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3e66cf332bc430de8285567ea13166eae76e7e1d"/></media></figure><para>
              In \(g(x)\), \(a\) is greater than/less than 50. </para>
          </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cd5259b9-f0b7-48fb-a1a4-bc137b5b7781" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="less than" data-solution-options="[&quot;greater than&quot;, &quot;less than&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>In \(g(x)\), \(b\) is greater than/less than 3. </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
  </section>
